{{also|schminke}}
==German==

===Etymology===
An originally [[Central German|Central]] and [[Low German]] word, from late {{der|de|gmh|smicke}}, {{m|gmh|smyncke||make-up}}, {{der|de|gml|sminke}}. Further origin uncertain, but probably related with {{m|de|schmeichen}}, {{cog|gml|smēken||to spread, stroke}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃmɪŋkə/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Schminke.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Schminken}}

# [[make-up]]
#: {{ux|de|Ich gehe immer ohne '''Schminke''' zur Arbeit.|I always go to work with no '''make-up''' on.}}

====Usage notes====
* ''Schminke'' and {{m|de|Make-up}} are principally synonymous, but the former is more likely to be used referring to the cosmetic substances, whereas ''Make-up'' is more likely to refer to the look that these substances create. Moreover, only ''Schminke'' is typically used in the context of carnival costumes and the like.

